      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Since sums of squares are very closely related to the variances accounted for by the various components of a particular linear model, it should not be surprising that hypothesis testing is based on the sums of squares. Such hypothesis tests can be quite involved, especially if we are evaluating the various components of a complex model. Here we consider the simplest case of testing the fit of the total model to the data.",
